{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Goto, From, and connection labels",
  "exampleId": "block-tags",
  "description": "The Goto [ref] takes the sine; both From [ref] blocks give it back on the far side of the sheet, without a wire, and the gains scale it by 2 and −1. Below, the label [VBUS] on the source joins the label [VBUS] by the load: one node, so the voltage sensor reads the 10 V of the source. The right-hand label is flipped so its terminal faces the load. Tags reach into the subsystems on a sheet, never out of them: a From inside a subsystem reads a Goto on its sheet or on any sheet above it, and a Goto inside a subsystem is not seen outside it. Set a tag in the block’s properties.",
  "duration": 1,
  "revision": 0,
